


# My Favourite Rainbows

The best rainbows come after a big rainstorm.

I love the moment when the sun peeps out from behind a grey cloud. The sky is still wet and dark on one side, but bright on the other. Then suddenly — there it is!

A huge arc of colour stretches across the sky. Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet. It looks like someone painted it with a giant brush.

My favourite rainbows are the ones I see over the fields near my house. They sit right on top of the green hills, and the colours look so bright against the dark clouds behind them.

Sometimes I see a second rainbow above the first one. It is fainter and the colours go the wrong way round. That always makes me gasp.

Mum says you can never reach the end of a rainbow. But I still like to try. I run across the wet grass, splashing through puddles in my wellies. The rainbow moves away every time I get close.

That is the magic of it. You can look, but you can never touch.

That is why I love rainbows the most. [end of text]


